@startuml DB-StablePackageBuildOnce
' ============================================================
' Diagram: Build-Once Stable Package — Full Lifecycle
' Purpose: Detailed step-by-step process for a database
'          package whose version.json has NO pre-release
'          label (i.e. it will produce a stable NuGet
'          package). Covers the complete path from the
'          developer's first schema change through all
'          BuildMaster promotion stages, final merge back
'          into the stable branch, and cleanup.
' Author:  Generated for Sprint-0007
' ============================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
skinparam NoteBorderColor #F9A825
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #888888
skinparam SequenceBoxBorderColor #888888
skinparam swimlaneBorderThickness 2

title "Build-Once Stable DB Package: Full Lifecycle\n(No pre-release label → eventual production merge)"

' ============================================================
' PHASE 1 — Developer sets stable version and writes migration
' ============================================================

|Developer Workstation|

start

:Checkout sprint worktree\n(branch: <N>-Sprint-NNNN-work-items);

:Edit Database/Flyway/SQL/\nV00.01.NNNNNN__<description>.sql;
note right
  New versioned Flyway migration.
  File name encodes the migration order.
  NEVER edit an already-applied migration.
end note

:Set version.json to stable version\n(no "-alpha", "-beta", or\n"-pre" label):
\n{
\n  "version": "1.5.0"
\n}
;
note right
  Nerdbank.GitVersioning (NBGV) uses
  version.json to compute the NuGet
  package version.
  A version with NO pre-release segment
  signals "this is a production-ready build."
  NBGV appends a build-height suffix only
  in CI; the base semver is clean (e.g. 1.5.0).
  Contrast with sprint-internal work that uses
  "version": "1.5.0-sprint0007" which always
  stays pre-release.
end note

:Test migration locally\nagainst Experimental DB\n(Rebuild-All.ps1 or manual Flyway migrate);

if (Local tests pass?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Fix migration SQL;
  backward :Re-run local test;
endif

:git add version.json + migration SQL file(s)\ngit commit -m "feat(db): stable migration 1.5.0 – <description>"\ngit push origin <sprint-branch>;

' ============================================================
' PHASE 2 — BuildMaster detects commit and starts pipeline
' ============================================================

|BuildMaster (CI Trigger)|

:Git webhook / polling detects\npush to sprint branch;

:Start pipeline:\n"ATAPUtilities-Database-Stable"\nfor commit <sha>;
note right
  BuildMaster identifies the pipeline
  to use based on the branch pattern
  and the version.json having no
  pre-release label.
  A separate pipeline handles sprint/alpha builds.
end note

' ============================================================
' PHASE 3 — Experimental stage
' ============================================================

|BM Stage: Experimental|

:Checkout source\n(repo + version.json);

:nbgv get-version → 1.5.0.<build-height>
\n(stable semver with CI build height);
note right
  NBGV computes: 1.5.0.42
  NuGet package version: 1.5.0.42
  (no pre-release segment)
end note

:Build NuGet package\n(nuget pack or dotnet pack)\nOutput: ATAPUtilities.Database.1.5.0.42.nupkg;

:Push .nupkg to ProGet\nfeed: atap-db-experimental;

:Provision Experimental DB from scratch\n(Rebuild-All.ps1 Experimental);

:Apply migration via Flyway\n(flyway migrate on Experimental instance);

:Run smoke tests\n(Verify/ folder SQL scripts);

if (Experimental tests pass?) then (yes)
  :Promote package to Development feed\n(ProGet: atap-db-experimental → atap-db-development);
  note right: Single .nupkg artifact is promoted;
else (fail)
  :BuildMaster marks stage FAILED;
  :Notify developer;
  stop
endif

' ============================================================
' PHASE 4 — Development stage
' ============================================================

|BM Stage: Development|

:Install .nupkg from ProGet\natap-db-development feed\n(same artifact, new feed);

:Apply Flyway migrations to\nDevelopment DB instance;

:Run development-level tests\n(Queries/ folder assertions);

if (Development tests pass?) then (yes)
  :Promote to Integration feed\n(ProGet: atap-db-development → atap-db-integration);
else (fail)
  :BuildMaster marks stage FAILED;
  :Notify developer;
  stop
endif

' ============================================================
' PHASE 5 — Integration stage
' ============================================================

|BM Stage: Integration|

:Integration DB was seeded from\nProduction backup at sprint start\n(Export-ProductionDatabaseForSprintInit.ps1);

:Install .nupkg from\nProGet: atap-db-integration;

:Apply Flyway migrations on top of\nproduction-seeded Integration DB\n(Incremental — only new V__ scripts);

:Run full integration test suite\n(Flyway + stored-proc assertions\nfrom StoredProcedures/);

if (Integration tests pass?) then (yes)
  :Promote to QA feed\n(ProGet: atap-db-integration → atap-db-qa);
else (fail)
  :BuildMaster marks stage FAILED;
  :Notify developer for remediation;
  stop
endif

' ============================================================
' PHASE 6 — QA stage (requires human approval gate)
' ============================================================

|BM Stage: QA|

:Install .nupkg from\nProGet: atap-db-qa;

:Apply Flyway migrations on\nQA DB (production snapshot);

:Run QA acceptance tests\n(manual or automated regression suite);

:Human approval gate:\nRelease Manager reviews migration and\ntest results before proceeding;

if (QA approved?) then (yes)
  :Promote to Production feed\n(ProGet: atap-db-qa → atap-db-production);
else (rejected)
  :Stage blocked — developer notified;
  :Create follow-up issue;
  stop
endif

' ============================================================
' PHASE 7 — Production deployment
' ============================================================

|BM Stage: Production|

:Install .nupkg from\nProGet: atap-db-production;

:Take pre-migration backup\nof Production DB\n(Backup-DbaDatabase via OtterScript);

:Apply Flyway migrations to\nProduction DB\n(flyway migrate -url=<prod>);

:Run production smoke tests\n(Verify/ folder scripts);

if (Production deployment succeeds?) then (yes)
  :Mark BuildMaster release\nas Deployed;
  :Tag Git commit with stable version\n(git tag v1.5.0.42);
else (fail)
  :Rollback: Restore-DbaDatabase\nfrom pre-migration backup;
  :Notify release manager + developer;
  stop
endif

' ============================================================
' PHASE 8 — Merge back to stable branch
' ============================================================

|Developer Workstation|

:Create Pull Request:\nsprint-branch → main\n(includes version.json + all migration SQL);

:PR review and merge via GitHub;
note right
  Squash-merge or regular merge depending
  on branch policy.
  The stable version tag (v1.5.0.42) is
  already on the merged commit SHA.
end note

:Delete sprint worktree\n(SprintEndAgent cleanup);

:main branch now contains\nstable migration 1.5.0\nfor next sprint baseline;

stop

' ============================================================
' Legend
' ============================================================
legend right
  |= Artifact |= Description |
  | version.json (no pre-release) | Signals a stable package build |
  | .nupkg (1.5.0.42) | Single immutable artifact promoted through feeds |
  | ProGet Feeds | atap-db-experimental → development → integration → qa → production |
  | Flyway | Incremental schema migration applied at each stage |
  | Human gate | QA approval required before Production promotion |
  | Rollback | Pre-migration production backup taken before deploy |
endlegend

@enduml
